<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan takes delivery of fourth French frigate.</title>
<headline>Taiwan takes delivery of fourth French frigate.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan on Monday took delivery of the fourth of six Lafayette-class frigates ordered from France, the state-funded Central News Agency said.</p>
<p>The agency quoted unidentified military sources as saying the 3,600-tonne Ti Hua frigate arrived in Taiwan after a 40-day voyage from France. The navy was expected to commission the ship later in August.</p>
<p>Taiwan, which has already commissioned three Lafayette-class frigates, ordered the French ships in 1991, saying it needed advanced weapons to counter the rapid military modernisation of China, the island's rival since a civil war split them in 1949.</p>
</text>
